  ('383446133562543298', 'Madame Bovary', 1991, 'Romance, Drama, History', 'Jean Rabier, Claude Chabrol', 'Claude Chabrol', 'Isabelle Huppert, Jean-François Balmer, Christophe Malavoy, Jean Yanne, Lucas Belvaux, Christiane Minazzoli, Jean-Louis Maury, Henri Attal', 'PG-13', 'In 19th-century France, doctor''s wife Emma Bovary seeks to escape her dull provincial life through various extramarital affairs and extravagant spending, leading to tragic consequences.', 'In 19th-century France, doctor''s wife Emma Bovary seeks to escape her dull provincial life through various extramarital affairs and extravagant spending, leading to tragic consequences.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/cBJtWAgDTCqxNJJOZjnRSh5Vxa5.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:2528'),
  ('967339683072028349', 'Madame Bovary', 2015, 'Drama', 'Sophie Barthes, Andrij Parekh, Dixie Chassay', 'Sophie Barthes, Felipe Marino', 'Mia Wasikowska, Rhys Ifans, Ezra Miller, Logan Marshall-Green, Henry Lloyd-Hughes, Laura Carmichael, Olivier Gourmet, Paul Giamatti', 'R', 'In 19th-century France, doctor''s wife Emma Bovary seeks to escape her dull provincial life through various extramarital affairs and extravagant spending, leading to tragic consequences.', 'In 19th-century France, doctor''s wife Emma Bovary seeks to escape her dull provincial life through various extramarital affairs and extravagant spending, leading to tragic consequences.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/jW0CRLVYOQm0HOh6fZXnW2JKxwF.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:253161'),
  ('1111501890888817234', 'Madame Butterfly', 1932, 'Drama', 'Marion Gering, David Abel', 'Joseph Moncure March, Josephine Lovett', 'Sylvia Sidney, Cary Grant, Charles Ruggles, Irving Pichel, Helen Jerome Eddy, Edmund Breese, Louise Carter, Judith Vosselli', null, 'Pinkerton marries Cho-Cho San in Japan, whilst on shore leave. When he leaves, she keeps his Japanese home as he left it. He returns three years later, having married again in America, and tells Cho-Cho that their affair is over. She has had a child in his absence, who is sent to her family, before she kills herself.', 'Pinkerton marries Cho-Cho San in Japan, whilst on shore leave. When he leaves, she keeps his Japanese home as he left it. He returns three years later, having married again in America, and tells Cho-Cho that their affair is over. She has had a child in his absence, who is sent to her family, before she kills herself.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/sFDLF2btxB2iQGy8A0ZyWl8BMzx.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:52356'),
  ('1095788472960148166', 'Madame Claude', 1977, 'Drama, Comedy', 'Just Jaeckin, Robert Fraisse', 'André G. Brunelin', 'Françoise Fabian, Dayle Haddon, Murray Head, Klaus Kinski, Vibeke Knudsen-Bergeron, Maurice Ronet, Robert Webber, Jean Gaven', null, 'Based on a true story. Madame Claude, a well connected Parisienne with dark past, runs a network of high-class call girls. She sends her girls to any place in the world to satisfy sexual desires of wealthy and powerful men. Claude''s manipulations also involve big business and politics. Meanwhile, photographer David Evans is trying to clear his own criminal record by providing the authorities with pictures of Claude''s girls with important clients in compromising positions. But powerful men can do anything to keep their secrets...', 'Based on a true story. Madame Claude, a well connected Parisienne with dark past, runs a network of high-class call girls. She sends her girls to any place in the world to satisfy sexual desires of wealthy and powerful men. Claude''s manipulations also involve big business and politics. Meanwhile, photographer David Evans is trying to clear his own criminal record by providing the authorities with pictures of Claude''s girls with important clients in compromising positions. But powerful men can do anything to keep their secrets...', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/fJ1GsC9eXjrWLEtnXI6TNML4xTn.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:194708'),
  ('99582282580942224', 'Madame Claude', 2021, 'Crime, Drama, Romance', 'Sylvie Verheyde', 'Sylvie Verheyde', 'Karole Rocher, Garance Marillier, Roschdy Zem, Pierre Deladonchamps, Liah O''Prey, Paul Hamy, Mylène Jampanoï, Hafsia Herzi', 'NR', 'Paris, the late 1960s. Madame Claude is at the head of a flourishing business dedicated to prostitution that gives her power over both the French political and criminal worlds. But the end of her empire is closer than she thinks.', 'Paris, the late 1960s. Madame Claude is at the head of a flourishing business dedicated to prostitution that gives her power over both the French political and criminal worlds. But the end of her empire is closer than she thinks.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/9miY5tHWmvVAft4gjqyaXyhLYHY.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:660006'),
  ('181077483917991856', 'Madame Curie', 1943, 'Drama, Romance, History', 'Mervyn LeRoy, Joseph Ruttenberg', 'Ève Curie', 'Greer Garson, Walter Pidgeon, Henry Travers, Albert Bassermann, Robert Walker, C. Aubrey Smith, May Whitty, Victor Francen', null, 'Poor physics student Marie is studying at the Sorbonne in 1890s Paris. One of the few women studying in her field, Marie encounters skepticism concerning her abilities, but is eventually offered a research placement in Pierre Curie''s lab. The scientists soon fall in love and embark on a shared quest to extract, from a particular type of rock, a new chemical element they have named radium. However, their research puts them on the brink of professional failure.', 'Poor physics student Marie is studying at the Sorbonne in 1890s Paris. One of the few women studying in her field, Marie encounters skepticism concerning her abilities, but is eventually offered a research placement in Pierre Curie''s lab. The scientists soon fall in love and embark on a shared quest to extract, from a particular type of rock, a new chemical element they have named radium. However, their research puts them on the brink of professional failure.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/mUKThJeC2WESwXfKf6tcAZn0B2g.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:37631'),
  ('307997292159579322', 'Madame de Sade', 1992, 'Drama, TV Movie', 'Ingmar Bergman, Per Norén, Bo Johansson', 'Yukio Mishima, Ingmar Bergman', 'Stina Ekblad, Anita Björk, Marie Richardson, Margaretha Byström, Agneta Ekmanner, Helena Brodin', null, 'This television production captures Ingmar Bergman’s stage adaptation of Yukio Mishima’s Madame de Sade, set in France from 1772 to the aftermath of the French Revolution. While the Marquis de Sade remains imprisoned, six women—including his wife Renée—debate his actions, reputation, and meaning, revealing conflicting views on devotion, morality, and power.', 'This television production captures Ingmar Bergman’s stage adaptation of Yukio Mishima’s Madame de Sade, set in France from 1772 to the aftermath of the French Revolution. While the Marquis de Sade remains imprisoned, six women—including his wife Renée—debate his actions, reputation, and meaning, revealing conflicting views on devotion, morality, and power.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/3nqSZ0bIYMWE9NOLRbXDRv0xoy6.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:47124'),
  ('188635593561220699', 'Madame de Sévigné', 2024, 'Drama, History', 'Isabelle Brocard, Philippe Rey, Georges Lechaptois', 'Yves Thomas, Isabelle Brocard', 'Karin Viard, Ana Girardot, Cédric Kahn, Noémie Lvovsky, Robin Renucci, Cyrille Mairesse, Antoine Prud''homme de la Boussinière, Alain Libolt', null, 'In the middle of the 17th century, the Marquise de Sévigné wanted to make her daughter a brilliant and independent woman in her own image. But the more she tries to control the young woman''s destiny, the more she alienates her. Mother and daughter then experience the throes of a singular and devastating passion. A major work of French literature is born from this devastation.', 'In the middle of the 17th century, the Marquise de Sévigné wanted to make her daughter a brilliant and independent woman in her own image. But the more she tries to control the young woman''s destiny, the more she alienates her. Mother and daughter then experience the throes of a singular and devastating passion. A major work of French literature is born from this devastation.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/v4satMrWuYPdTTB4nP0LKxQmZRP.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:960135'),
  ('359216786262370362', 'Madame Death', 1969, 'Horror, Mystery, Science Fiction', 'Jaime Salvador, Alfredo Uribe, Tito Novaro', 'Ramón Obón', 'Regina Torné, John Carradine, Elsa Cárdenas, Miguel Ángel Álvarez, Isela Vega, Víctor Junco, Carlos Ancira, Mario Orea', null, 'A mad scientist teams with an evil, disfigured woman to kidnap and operate on young women to make her look beautiful again.', 'A mad scientist teams with an evil, disfigured woman to kidnap and operate on young women to make her look beautiful again.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/cx7TqaHMo3TGa2XWgwC3XIcfHV.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:174745'),
  ('286970789122181276', 'Madame Doubtfire', 2001, 'Comedy, TV Movie', 'Eric Civanyan, Daniel Roussel', 'Leslie Dixon, Randi Mayem Singer', 'Michel Leeb, Josy Bernard, Francis Lemaire, Jordy Serras, Rachel Arditi, Idwig Stephane, Tom Leeb, Maylis Merchet', null, 'French TV-Movie based on the classic American comedy classic Mrs. Doubtfire.', 'French TV-Movie based on the classic American comedy classic Mrs. Doubtfire.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/ja0ArbKKMrbLt7DJkKAL7i9moZn.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:179792'),
  ('358244442521913984', 'Madame DuBarry', 1919, 'Drama, History', 'Ernst Lubitsch, Fritz Arno Wagner, Theodor Sparkuhl', 'Norbert Falk, Hanns Kräly', 'Pola Negri, Emil Jannings, Harry Liedtke, Reinhold Schünzel, Eduard von Winterstein, Else Berna, Fred Immler, Gustav Czimeg', null, 'The story of Madame DuBarry, the mistress of Louis XV of France, and her loves in the time of the French revolution.', 'The story of Madame DuBarry, the mistress of Louis XV of France, and her loves in the time of the French revolution.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/cRyZz3Rz3WfyGaSRnaxnrGBBafT.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:48218'),
  ('800406346454020957', 'Madame Freedom', 1956, 'Drama', 'Lee Han-chan, Han Hyeong-mo, Seong-hwi Lee', null, 'Park Am, Kim Jeong-rim, No Gyeong-hui, Ju Seon-tae, Kim Dong-won, Go Hyang-mi, Yang Mi-hee, Lee Min', null, 'Oh starts working at a boutique to help her make a living. Professor Jang begins dating the typist Miss Park, but decides to break up with her to protect her family. Han''s wife anonymously sends a letter to Jang to reveal Oh''s affair.', 'Oh starts working at a boutique to help her make a living. Professor Jang begins dating the typist Miss Park, but decides to break up with her to protect her family. Han''s wife anonymously sends a letter to Jang to reveal Oh''s affair.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/mknsbMQFN78jVNC021fTSuEw1Rj.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:264692'),
  ('133386417156359289', 'Madame Hofmann', 2024, 'Documentary', 'Sébastien Lifshitz', 'Sébastien Lifshitz', 'Sylvie Hofmann', null, '"Welcome to my life", Sylvie Hofmann repeats this sentence almost all day long. Sylvie has been a nurse for 40 years at the North Hospital of Marseille. Her life is running. Between patients, her sick mother, her husband and her daughter, she has always devoted her life to helping others. What if she decided to think a little about herself? To retire? Does she have the right, but above all, does she really want to?', '"Welcome to my life", Sylvie Hofmann repeats this sentence almost all day long. Sylvie has been a nurse for 40 years at the North Hospital of Marseille. Her life is running. Between patients, her sick mother, her husband and her daughter, she has always devoted her life to helping others. What if she decided to think a little about herself? To retire? Does she have the right, but above all, does she really want to?', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/rX03DtKD0LiV3DkwCrzz7goAz4b.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:1157419'),
  ('1127983596955706932', 'Madame Irma', 2006, 'Comedy', 'Didier Bourdon, Yves Fajnberg', 'Didier Bourdon', 'Didier Bourdon, Pascal Légitimus, Arly Jover, Catherine Mouchet, Julie Ferrier, Yoann Denaive, Jacques Herlin, Claire Nadeau', null, 'Francis, who is in his forties, manages the French subsidiary of an American high-tech company. But the shareholders suddenly decide to close it. Depressed by the idea of being unemployed and the prospect of losing his second wife, Francis decides to consult a fortune-teller. The experience is a real eye-opener for him and the start of a new career: He pretends to be a fortune teller himself and turns into Madame Irma. How to explain that to his wife Clotilde?', 'Francis, who is in his forties, manages the French subsidiary of an American high-tech company. But the shareholders suddenly decide to close it. Depressed by the idea of being unemployed and the prospect of losing his second wife, Francis decides to consult a fortune-teller. The experience is a real eye-opener for him and the start of a new career: He pretends to be a fortune teller himself and turns into Madame Irma. How to explain that to his wife Clotilde?', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/3JmXXkpiPXjCst15oV9uv31wfBQ.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:43617'),
  ('769299405982441151', 'Madame Mayor', 1960, 'Comedy', 'Roviros Manthoulis, Tasos Karabelas, Despina Kontogiorgou', 'Nestoras Matsas, Vion Papamihalis', 'Georgia Vasileiadou, Vasilis Avlonitis, Aleka Stratigou, Koula Agagiotou, Nikos Fermas, Athina Tzimouli, Nikos Kourkoulos, Asi Mihailidou', null, 'On the square of a village on a beautiful greek island there are two competing tavernas. One belongs to Aspasia and the other to Anargyros, who is a former Sergeant Major of the Greek Army. Their constant conflict doesn’t affect their children, who love and meet each other in secret. The local elections creates a new battlefield for the two taverna-owners, as they both run for office and promise everything to everyone.', 'On the square of a village on a beautiful greek island there are two competing tavernas. One belongs to Aspasia and the other to Anargyros, who is a former Sergeant Major of the Greek Army. Their constant conflict doesn’t affect their children, who love and meet each other in secret. The local elections creates a new battlefield for the two taverna-owners, as they both run for office and promise everything to everyone.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/tn0uA7YsgwcV5CCz53kuq7MBmBx.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:332064'),
  ('282952291084449151', 'Madame Rosa', 1977, 'Drama, Comedy', 'Moshé Mizrahi, Tony Aboyantz, Emmanuel Fonlladosa', 'Moshé Mizrahi', 'Simone Signoret, Michal Bat-Adam, Gabriel Jabbour, Mohamed Zinet, Costa-Gavras, Nadia Samir, Samy Ben-Youb, Bernard Lajarrige', null, 'Madame Rosa lives in a sixth-floor walkup in the Pigalle; she''s a retired prostitute, Jewish and an Auschwitz survivor, a foster mom to children of other prostitutes. Momo is the oldest and her favorite, an Algerian lad whom she raises as a Muslim. He asks about his parents; she answers evasively. As she ages and takes fewer children, Momo must do more for her; as money is tight, he tries to earn pennies on the street with a puppet. He''s a beautiful man-child, and Madame Rosa makes him promise never to sell himself or become a pimp. A film editor, Nadine, befriends him, and his father appears as well. Madame Rosa reaches her last days in fear of hospitals, and Momo must act.', 'Madame Rosa lives in a sixth-floor walkup in the Pigalle; she''s a retired prostitute, Jewish and an Auschwitz survivor, a foster mom to children of other prostitutes. Momo is the oldest and her favorite, an Algerian lad whom she raises as a Muslim. He asks about his parents; she answers evasively. As she ages and takes fewer children, Momo must do more for her; as money is tight, he tries to earn pennies on the street with a puppet. He''s a beautiful man-child, and Madame Rosa makes him promise never to sell himself or become a pimp. A film editor, Nadine, befriends him, and his father appears as well. Madame Rosa reaches her last days in fear of hospitals, and Momo must act.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/o2yCU9XwakKnpD33D8TxenRSiNM.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:42223'),
  ('141550193090285964', 'Madame Satã', 2002, 'Crime, Drama, Romance, History', 'Karim Aïnouz, Walter Carvalho', 'Sérgio Machado, Mauricio Zacharias, Karim Aïnouz', 'Lázaro Ramos, Marcélia Cartaxo, Flávio Bauraqui, Renata Sorrah, Fellipe Marques, Emiliano Queiroz, Gero Camilo, Floriano Peixoto', null, 'In the favelas of Rio de Janeiro of the 1930s, João Francisco dos Santos is several things — son of slaves, ex-convict, thug, homosexual and adopted father for a number of pariahs. João expresses himself on the stage of a cabaret as Madame Satã.', 'In the favelas of Rio de Janeiro of the 1930s, João Francisco dos Santos is several things — son of slaves, ex-convict, thug, homosexual and adopted father for a number of pariahs. João expresses himself on the stage of a cabaret as Madame Satã.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/rgsrsLJXzzmMiTvatmEhXU8fMY2.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:46993'),
  ('855799913518707210', 'Madame Sin', 1972, 'Action, TV Movie, Thriller', 'David Greene, Anthony B. Richmond', null, 'Bette Davis, Robert Wagner, Denholm Elliott, Gordon Jackson, Dudley Sutton, Catherine Schell, Paul Maxwell, David Healy', null, 'A CIA agent is used as a pawn in an insane woman''s plan to steal a Polaris submarine.', 'A CIA agent is used as a pawn in an insane woman''s plan to steal a Polaris submarine.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/6wJKkpiewKW5jt8ggGE83nd1jCM.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:55032'),
  ('215988565295412399', 'Madame Sousatzka', 1988, 'Drama, Music', 'John Schlesinger, Nat Crosby, John Dodds', 'John Schlesinger, Ruth Prawer Jhabvala', 'Shirley MacLaine, Navin Chowdhry, Shabana Azmi, Peggy Ashcroft, Twiggy, Leigh Lawson, Geoffrey Bayldon, Lee Montague', 'PG-13', 'In London, eccentric piano instructor Madame Sousatzka takes on a new prize protégé, Manek, a teenage Bengali immigrant who displays incredible talent. Manek forms a close bond with his teacher, but soon discovers that she expects her pupils to become disciplined in all areas of life, and not just behind the piano. As he struggles to meet the challenges, Manek must also deal with his mother, who vies with his teacher for his attention.', 'In London, eccentric piano instructor Madame Sousatzka takes on a new prize protégé, Manek, a teenage Bengali immigrant who displays incredible talent. Manek forms a close bond with his teacher, but soon discovers that she expects her pupils to become disciplined in all areas of life, and not just behind the piano. As he struggles to meet the challenges, Manek must also deal with his mother, who vies with his teacher for his attention.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/iXBUkgTfFzT9OC9B4egsF0rSAPr.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:118098'),
  ('1124355341005529767', 'Madame Tutli-Putli', 2007, 'Animation, Thriller', 'Chris Lavis, Maciek Szczerbowski, David Bryant', 'Chris Lavis, Maciek Szczerbowski', 'Laurie Maher', null, 'Madame Tutli-Putli boards the Night Train, weighed down with all her earthly possessions and the ghosts of her past. She travels alone, facing both the kindness and menace of strangers. As day descends into dark, she finds herself caught up in a desperate metaphysical adventure.', 'Madame Tutli-Putli boards the Night Train, weighed down with all her earthly possessions and the ghosts of her past. She travels alone, facing both the kindness and menace of strangers. As day descends into dark, she finds herself caught up in a desperate metaphysical adventure.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/lLEvanzHSpvbTpKpTfKuGAUOl91.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:35253'),
  ('648540790572423183', 'Madame Web', 2024, 'Action, Fantasy', 'Andrew Stahl, Lindsey Moran, Cary Lee', 'S.J. Clarkson, Claire Parker, Matt Sazama', 'Dakota Johnson, Sydney Sweeney, Isabela Merced, Celeste O''Connor, Tahar Rahim, Mike Epps, Emma Roberts, Adam Scott', 'PG-13', 'Forced to confront revelations about her past, paramedic Cassandra Webb forges a relationship with three young women destined for powerful futures...if they can all survive a deadly present.', 'Forced to confront revelations about her past, paramedic Cassandra Webb forges a relationship with three young women destined for powerful futures...if they can all survive a deadly present.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/rULWuutDcN5NvtiZi4FRPzRYWSh.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:634492'),
  ('817915728817007966', 'Madame X', 1966, 'Drama, Crime', 'David Lowell Rich, Douglas Green, Russell Metty', 'Jean Holloway', 'Lana Turner, John Forsythe, Constance Bennett, Ricardo Montalban, Burgess Meredith, Keir Dullea, John van Dreelen, Virginia Grey', 'NR', 'Holly Parker, the wife of a wealthy diplomat, is compromised by the accidental death of a man who has been romantically pursuing her. She is forced by her mother-in-law to assume a new identity in order to save the reputation of her husband and infant son. She wanders the world, trying to forget her heartbreak with the aid of alcohol and unsavory men. Eventually returning to the city of her downfall, she murders a blackmailer who threatens to expose her past. Amazingly, Holly is represented at her murder trial by her now adult son, who has become a public defender. In the hope of protecting her family, she refuses to reveal her real name and is known to the court as "Madame X".', 'Holly Parker, the wife of a wealthy diplomat, is compromised by the accidental death of a man who has been romantically pursuing her. She is forced by her mother-in-law to assume a new identity in order to save the reputation of her husband and infant son. She wanders the world, trying to forget her heartbreak with the aid of alcohol and unsavory men. Eventually returning to the city of her downfall, she murders a blackmailer who threatens to expose her past. Amazingly, Holly is represented at her murder trial by her now adult son, who has become a public defender. In the hope of protecting her family, she refuses to reveal her real name and is known to the court as "Madame X".', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/pF9m0GruyTuC4H4cBROEzEaf42C.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:42723'),
  ('1142219828114412999', 'Madame X – An Absolute Ruler', 1978, 'Fantasy', 'Ulrike Ottinger, Tabea Blumenschein, Frank Ripploh', 'Ulrike Ottinger', 'Tabea Blumenschein, Roswitha Janz, Monika von Cube, Irena von Lichtenstein, Yvonne Rainer, Hella Utesch, Lutze , Ulrike Ottinger', null, 'The notorious pirate ruler Madame X places a print ad, calling on women to escape their boring lives and promising "gold, love and adventure" to all who come aboard her ship, the Orlando. A motley crew including a housewife, diva and artist (played by Yvonne Rainer) embark on a quest for self-transformation, which quickly heads towards destruction as they are subjected to Madame X''s sadistic, erotic escapades.', 'The notorious pirate ruler Madame X places a print ad, calling on women to escape their boring lives and promising "gold, love and adventure" to all who come aboard her ship, the Orlando. A motley crew including a housewife, diva and artist (played by Yvonne Rainer) embark on a quest for self-transformation, which quickly heads towards destruction as they are subjected to Madame X''s sadistic, erotic escapades.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/muVjWtqIsAz7YbF4aCBZqGoWahA.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:130962'),
